  "question": {
    "text": "If $U_n(n=1,2)$ denote the $n^{\\text {th }}$ derivative $(n=1,2)$ of $U(x)=\\frac{L x+M}{x^2-2 B x+C}(L, M, B, C$ are constants $)$, then $P U_2+Q U_1$ $+R U=0$, holds for",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CLZOx",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{x}^2-2 \\mathrm{~B}, \\mathrm{Q}=2 \\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{R}=3 \\mathrm{x}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "58jlc",
      "text": "$P=x^2-2 B x+C, Q=4((x-B), R=2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SVBRS",
      "text": "$P=2 x, Q=2 B, R=2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZyICx",
      "text": "$P=x^2, Q=x, R=3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Hint: } U(x)=\\frac{L x+m}{x^2-2 B x+c}, U(x)\\left(x^2-2 B x+c\\right)=L x+m \\\\ & U(x)(2 x-2 B)+\\left(x^2-2 B x+c\\right) U_1(x)=L \\\\ & U(x)2 \\times 2(2 x-2 B) U_1(x)+(2 x-2 B) U_1(x)+\\left(x^2-2 B x+c\\right) U_2(x)=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow U_2\\left(x^2-2 Bx+c\\right)+U_1(4 x-4 B)+2 U=0 \\\\ & \\therefore P=x^2-2 B x+c, Q=4(x-B), R=2\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
